---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import family from '../assets/family.jpg';
---

<section id="about" class="border-t border-line">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-start gap-10 px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 md:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr] md:gap-16 md:py-28">
    <Image
      src={family}
      alt="Kenny Picavet with his family"
      widths={[320, 640]}
      sizes="(min-width: 768px) 320px, 100vw"
      class="aspect-[4/5] w-full max-w-xs rounded-md object-cover"
    />
    <div class="max-w-[62ch]">
      <h2 class="mb-6 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight md:text-4xl">Outside of work</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <p>
          I live in Beveren with my family. Most weekends I’m on the sidelines: my eldest plays
          basketball, my youngest is set on becoming a football pro.
        </p>
        <p>
          When it’s quiet, we build LEGO together, following the instructions, mostly. I’d rather eat
          out than cook. And I’ve supported Anderlecht long enough to have learned a lot about patience.
        </p>
        <p>
          My first real project, as an intern in 2011, was a CV generator: consultants entered their
          experience once and got a clean CV in one click. This site works the same way. The page you’re
          reading and <a href="/cv" class="text-ink underline underline-offset-4">my CV</a> come from one
          data file.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
